# Private documents, by name and in any letter case. This only keeps them out of `git add`; tools/privacy_guard.py is the
# enforcement. The negated lines keep ordinary English words that happen to contain the same letters.
*[Tt][Hh][Ee][Ss][Ii][Ss]*
!*[Pp]arenthesis*
!*[Hh]ypothesis*
!*[Ss]ynthesis*
!*[Aa]naesthesis*
!*[Aa]nesthesis*
# A source file may be named after what it benchmarks. Its content is scanned like any other, and a directory stays ignored.
!*[Tt][Hh][Ee][Ss][Ii][Ss]*.rs
!*[Tt][Hh][Ee][Ss][Ii][Ss]*.py
!*[Tt][Hh][Ee][Ss][Ii][Ss]*.sh
!*[Tt][Hh][Ee][Ss][Ii][Ss]*.toml
*[Mm][Aa][Ss][Tt][Ee][Rr][Aa][Rr][Bb][Ee][Ii][Tt]*
*.local.*

target/
refs/
*.fmt
/.rstex-cache/
tests/cd/2[12]-*.tex
# Runner output belongs under target/. These names only keep a stray copy out of `git add`.
results.jsonl
results.json
/tests/corpus/results/
/tests/expected/
__pycache__/
/refs
.claude/
tests/cd/out/
# A case's output, from a run in tests/integration by hand.  The documents are what is committed.
tests/integration/**/*.log
tests/integration/**/*.pdf
tests/integration/**/*.dvi
tests/integration/**/*.aux
tests/integration/**/*.vf
tests/integration/**/*.tfm
tests/integration/**/*.pl
